# 🌍 Individuals & Societies Weekly Study Log

## What I Learned

This week in I&S, we had a debate about whether constitutional monarchies should continue to exist.

My position developed during the debate. Instead of arguing that monarchy should simply be abolished, I argued that a constitutional monarchy could coexist with modern democracy, similar to the UK system.

I argued that separating a symbolic head of state from the elected government could help prevent too much political power from being concentrated in one person. I also used tourism as an economic argument for keeping a monarchy, although I still need to verify the exact statistics I used.

## What Went Well

I enjoyed this debate because I had the chance to have a serious discussion and respond to different arguments.

I was able to explain my main position and continue developing my argument during the debate instead of only repeating what I had prepared.

## Where I Got Stuck

I struggled when I had to respond immediately to one of the opposing arguments.

At one point, I forgot exactly what the other person had said and did not know how to reply. Because of that, I continued with my own argument instead of directly answering their point.

## How I Dealt With It

I kept the discussion moving and continued explaining my side rather than stopping completely.

However, I realised that this avoided the difficult argument instead of actually answering it.

## What I Need to Improve Next Week

I need to improve my improvisation and rebuttal skills.

Instead of relying mainly on a prepared script, I want to listen more carefully to the other side, identify their main claim, and respond directly to it.
